# ${{ values.name }}

${{ values.description }}

Created from the Internal Developer Platform's Node.js service template. The
delivery path, container hardening and Kubernetes contract come from the
platform; what belongs to this repository is the code in `src/` and its tests.

## Run it

```bash
npm install
npm start          # http://127.0.0.1:8080
npm test
```

| Route | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `/` | Service identity and version |
| `/healthz` | Liveness. Never depends on a downstream, so one slow dependency cannot restart every pod |
| `/readyz` | Readiness. Returns 503 while draining, so traffic stops before the socket closes |

## How it ships

1. Open a pull request. CI runs the tests, builds the container, smoke tests it
   under the same restrictions Kubernetes applies, and scans it for high and
   critical vulnerabilities.
2. Merge it. The image is published to Amazon ECR and addressed by digest.
3. A promotion pull request appears against the platform repository containing
   the new digest. Merging that is what deploys; reverting it is what rolls back.

Deployment state lives in the platform repository, not here, so a change to this
repository cannot deploy itself.

## What this repository does not contain

The Helm chart, the Argo CD Application and the cluster configuration are owned
by the platform team and shared by every service. To change how this service
runs — replicas, resources, probes — open a pull request against the platform
repository rather than adding a chart here.

